%I A401172 #16 Oct 23 2026 17:20:17
%S A401172 2,7,12,17,22,27,32,37
%N A401172 a(n) = floor(-log_10(kappa(n))), where kappa(n) is the infimum of Q(f)/||f||^2 over nonzero smooth f(u) supported in (-log(n)/2, log(n)/2), Q being the Weil quadratic form of the Riemann zeta function; a(n) = 0 if kappa(n) <= 0.
%C A401172 Q(f) = 2*Re(F(i/2)*conj(F(-i/2))) + (1/(2*Pi))*Integral_{-oo..oo} (Re(psi(1/4 + i*t/2)) - log(Pi))*|F(t)|^2 dt - Sum_{p^k} 2*log(p)*p^(-k/2)*Re(Integral f(u + k*log(p))*conj(f(u)) du), with F(t) = Integral f(u)*exp(i*t*u) du, ||f||^2 = Integral |f(u)|^2 du, psi = digamma, u = log(x).
%C A401172 All terms are proved (computer-assisted): 10^(-a(n)-1) < kappa(n) <= 10^(-a(n)). The upper bounds for 3 <= n <= 9 are certified in Appendix B of the Wiktorowicz and Wiktorowicz link; the lower bounds and the case n = 2 are unpublished.
%C A401172 Since kappa(n) is nonincreasing, kappa(n) > 0 for 2 <= n <= 16: Theorem B (Liu link) covers n <= 8, and an unpublished interval-arithmetic proof by the same method extends this to n = 16.
%C A401172 An explicit g(u) supported in (-log(11)/2, log(11)/2) gives Q(g)/||g||^2 <= 8.62132*10^(-49) (Wiktorowicz and Wiktorowicz link, Appendix B), so a(11) >= 48 (since kappa(11) > 0) and the pattern a(n) = 5*n - 8 (2 <= n <= 9) fails at n = 11.
%C A401172 For every n >= 3, kappa(n) <= C*(1 + d*sqrt(n))*n^(29/2)*exp(-4*Pi*n) unconditionally, with C = 3.03*10^6 and d <= 6.40*10^(-11), and d = 0 under the Riemann Hypothesis (Wiktorowicz and Wiktorowicz link, Theorem 1). Lower bounds for kappa(n) are not addressed there.
%D A401172 André Weil, Sur les "formules explicites" de la théorie des nombres premiers, Meddel. Lunds Univ. Mat. Sem., Suppl.-band M. Riesz (1952), 252-265.
%H A401172 Alain Connes and Caterina Consani, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.13771">Weil positivity and trace formula, the archimedean place</a>, arXiv:2006.13771 [math.NT], 2020.
%H A401172 Alain Connes and Caterina Consani, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.01715">Spectral triples and zeta-cycles</a>, arXiv:2106.01715 [math.NT], 2021.
%H A401172 Vincent Liu, <a href="https://www.alphaxiv.org/abs/2609.weil-positivity-riemann-zeta-bounds">Certified Weil Positivity Beyond the Unit Window</a>, alphaXiv preprint, 2026.
%H A401172 Rafał Wiktorowicz and Braun SI Wiktorowicz, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23447303">An Unconditional Exponential Upper Bound for the Windowed Weil Quadratic Form</a>, Zenodo preprint, 2026.
%F A401172 If kappa(n) > 0, then a(n) >= floor(4*Pi*n/log(10) - (29/2)*log_10(n) - log_10(3.03*10^6*(1 + 6.4*10^(-11)*sqrt(n)))) for n >= 3.
%Y A401172 Cf. A016873.
%K A401172 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401172 2,1
